{"id":16558,"name":"Cherokee County","slug":"cherokee-county","state":"Georgia","code":"GA","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/redeemable-tax-deed/redeemable-tax-deed-states/georgia-redeemable-tax-deed-90-off-real-estate-value/cherokee-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-02-04T07:19:06","facts":{"taxSaleType":"Redeemable Tax Deeds","typicalSaleDate":"First Tuesday of each month","redemptionPeriod":"12 months","interestRate":"20% for the first year, 10% for each subsequent year","bidProcedure":"Premium Bid","extra":[{"label":"Auction Site","value":"Cherokee County Courthouse, Canton, GA"},{"label":"Sale Contact","value":"Denise Mastroserio, Tax Commissioner, (678) 493-6400"},{"label":"County Website","value":"County Website"},{"label":"Tax Deed Info","value":"Cherokee County Tax Sales"}]},"bodyHtml":"\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed aligncenter is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"BAnmmoKbY9ROGc1052186CZNaHjvPur7eXzyxckIRJyVEUge476DfSrpXFOzGiaQf\"><iframe title=\"Cherokee County | Georgia Tax Deed Investing | Holding Your Deed Title for 50% Profit\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/Xnj7j_O4lpw?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:31px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Maximize-Your-Returns:-Let-Your-Investment-Roll-Over-for-Larger-Profits-in-Cherokee-County!\">Let Your Investment Roll Over for Larger Profits in Cherokee County!</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Investing in smaller counties like Cherokee County, <a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/redeemable-tax-deed/redeemable-tax-deed-states/georgia-redeemable-tax-deed-90-off-real-estate-value/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Georgia</mark></a>, has unique advantages. With a population of over 258,000, Cherokee offers a manageable market for investors. The smaller scale allows for thorough research within the four-week window from listing to auction, which is crucial for tax deed investing.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"How-Does-Tax-Deed-Investing-Work-in-Cherokee-County?\">How Does Tax Deed Investing Work in Cherokee County?</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Cherokee County uses Redeemable Deeds. Here&#8217;s how it works:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Delinquent Taxes:</strong> The county issues a tax lien when a property owner falls behind on taxes.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Tax Sale: </strong>The county auctions the property if the owner doesn&#8217;t pay the taxes.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Redemption Period</strong>: The owner or interested parties have 12 months to reclaim the property by paying the initial bid, additional taxes, and a 20% premium for the first year, plus 10% for each subsequent year.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Foreclosure</strong>: After 12 months, the purchaser can foreclose on the right to redeem and become the property&#8217;s new owner.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Important-Details\">Important Details</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Steps-to-Start-Tax-Deed-Investing\">Steps to Start Tax Deed Investing in Cherokee County</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Research Local Laws</strong>: Understand the legal framework and key regulations.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Visit the Treasurer&#8217;s Website</strong>: Access information about tax sales.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Check the Auction Site</strong>: Visit the <a href=\"https://www.cherokeecountytax.com/tax-sales.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Superior Court building</mark></a> for auction details.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Read About Tax Deeds</strong>: Understand the sale schedule, parcel inquiry, and other essentials.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Contact the County Office</strong>: For additional inquiries, contact Denise Mastroserio at (678) 493-6400.</p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Cherokee-County-Justice-Center.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Cherokee-County-Justice-Center-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Cherokee-County-Justice-Center-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Cherokee-County-Justice-Center-768x512.webp 768w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Cherokee-County-Justice-Center-20x13.webp 20w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Cherokee-County-Justice-Center-32x21.webp 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Cherokee-County-Justice-Center.png\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Cherokee-County-Justice-Center.png 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Cherokee-County-Justice-Center-541x360.png 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Cherokee-County-Justice-Center-296x197.png 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Cherokee-County-Justice-Center-768x512.png 768w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Cherokee-County-Justice-Center-20x13.png 20w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Cherokee-County-Justice-Center-32x21.png 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-16570 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"Cherokee County Justice Center\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:31px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Pro-Tips\">Pro Tips</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Detailed Research</strong>: Ensure thorough property research to avoid complications.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Title Examination</strong>: Check for outstanding liens or encumbrances.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Foreclosure Awareness</strong>: Be aware that errors can void sales, requiring proactive attention to potential issues.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Cherokee-County-Highlights\">Cherokee County Highlights</h2>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Popular Attractions</strong>: Explore parks, theatres, and historic sites.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Transportation Infrastructure</strong>: Benefit from well-developed roads, rails, and nearby airports.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Economic Development</strong>: Growth in sectors like technology and manufacturing.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Community Appeal</strong>: Enjoy outdoor activities, entertainment, and historical attractions.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Frequently-Asked-Questions\">Frequently Asked Questions</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: What happens if the property is not redeemed within the 12-month period?</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>A: The purchaser can foreclose on the right to redeem and take ownership of the property.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: Can I make improvements to the property during the redemption period?</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>A: No, improvements cannot be made until the redemption period ends and foreclosure is completed.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: How often are tax sales held in Cherokee County?</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>A: Tax sales are typically held on the first Tuesday of each month.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>For more detailed information, visit the <a href=\"https://www.cherokeega.com/Tax-Commissioners-Office/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Cherokee County Tax Commissioner&#8217;s Office</mark></a><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\"> </mark>and the <a href=\"https://www.cherokeecountytax.com/tax-sales.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Cherokee County Tax Sales Page</mark></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Need-a-Hand?\">Need a Hand?</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>We&#8217;re here to help you with your tax lien investing journey. Feel free to <a href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_